  "executive_briefing": "As of August 2026, crypto market structure is undergoing significant legislative and technical evolutions driven by the US Senate's procedural advancement of the CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633). Regulatory definitions establishing digital commodities and securities are clearing structural roadblocks for mainstream financial institutions. Meanwhile, spot Bitcoin ETFs have entered a period of maturation and normalized flow dynamics following massive early accumulation, transitioning BTC from a speculative vehicle to a standard asset allocation. On the technical front, Ethereum maintains its structural dominance over smart contract execution and enterprise tokenization via its EVM ecosystem, while decentralized cross-chain liquidity protocols are unlocking native trustless swaps between BTC and ETH, eliminating reliance on vulnerable wrapped tokens and bridging Bitcoin's store-of-value liquidity into multi-chain DeFi ecosystems.",
